  "_unbounded": {
    "decay": "the reference's usable decay span is 0.015-0.035 s, which is 3 to 7 points on the envelope's 5 ms hop and under the 9 `measure_note` needs to fit a slope, so `decay_db_s` is absent on 25 of 25 reference rows. Measured off the corpus, the reference falls 60 dB within 40 ms of its peak. The model's span is 0.060-0.065 s - it rings 1.86 to 4.33 times longer than the reference, and with no rate on the reference side nothing here holds that.",
    "aftersound": "as `decay`. `double_decay` needs 12 envelope points and the reference's span holds 3 to 7, so `decay_late_db_s` is absent on 25 of 25 reference rows.",
    "doubling": "as `decay`. `double_decay` never runs on the reference, so the prompt-minus-aftersound gap is absent on 25 of 25 reference rows and there is no pair to difference.",
    "body": "the 0.2-1.2 s body window opens 165 ms after the reference has already fallen 60 dB. Read off the corpus WAVs, that segment is exactly digital zero - absolute maximum 0.000e+00, RMS -240 dBFS - so both bands of `body_below_f0_db` are 0 and it returns nothing on 25 of 25 reference rows.",
    "partial_tilt": "as `decay`. Fitting a per-partial decay rate needs the same envelope points the free-fall slope does, so `partial_decay_db_s` is eight NaNs on 25 of 25 reference rows and there is no rate to split into high and low."
  },
